  I feel that the kitchen sink should be eliminated. A new fountain/sink type should be created in it's place.I propose the culdron
(*spelling may be wrong*)

  You could pour multiple potions into a culdron. This in turn would cause a mixing effect.  You could ignite a culdron with fire.
This would boil the contents of the culdron. A player could add monster corpses to the mixture.
Culdron recepies could be given by the oracle.

  The boiling of monster might be considered very simular to tinning a corpse, but just imagine throwing a potion of boiled cockatrice
at the wizard of yendor!

  When a potion is emptied with the #pour or #empty command the flask could be kept and represented as an 'empty potion'.
Also a water jug or canteen object class could be created!  (ps. I perfer the #pour command.)

  If you add lots of water to a burning culdron you should be able to fill more than one empty potion with the culdron's contents.

  A potion derived from a culdron should be given the class either a 'man-made potion' or just 'A potion'.

  Culdrens could have alignment.

  If a character is strong enough could be picked up. Only with gloves if the culdron is hot.

  Drinking from a hot culdron may cause HP damage.

  How about a new room type.   "The Witches Coven"

  Also a potion of oil could be drunk. If you come in contact with open flame 
you should be able to breath fire.  Also dipping
cursed objects into the potion of oil could cause the object to slip off.

